<section class="membermissions-section">
  <h2 class="membermissions-title">missions and nuggets</h2>
  <p class="membermissions-intro">
    Twennie gives you more than learning units. It also helps you spot opportunities, organize action, and build momentum around the work that matters most.
  </p>

  <div class="membermissions-grid">

    <!-- Mission Control -->
    <div class="membermissions-card">
      <div class="membermissions-imagewrap">
        <img src="/images/spybluey.png" alt="Spy Bluey">
      </div>

      <div class="membermissions-content">
        <h3 class="membermissions-cardtitle">mission control</h3>
        <p class="membermissions-text">
          Mission Control is where learning turns into action. Missions help teams focus on a goal, assign meaningful work, and move ideas forward instead of letting them fade into good intentions.
        </p>
        <p class="membermissions-text">
          Whether the mission is learning-focused, research-based, business development related, or tied to internal improvement, Mission Control helps create structure, accountability, and progress.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The Mine -->
    <div class="membermissions-card">
      <div class="membermissions-imagewrap">
        <img src="/images/minerbluey.png" alt="Miner Bluey">
      </div>

      <div class="membermissions-content">
        <h3 class="membermissions-cardtitle">the mine</h3>
        <p class="membermissions-text">
          The Mine is where Twennie Nuggets live. Nuggets are short, useful pieces of intelligence that help you notice projects, trends, client activity, and market movement earlier.
        </p>
        <p class="membermissions-text">
          Instead of waiting for opportunities to become obvious, Nuggets help you collect signals, track what matters, and build awareness over time. They turn scattered information into something your team can actually use.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="membermissions-note">
    <p>
      These features are available through Twennie’s group environment, where leaders and members can work together, assign learning, and coordinate action.
